# Copy this file to .env and fill in real values — .env is gitignored.
#
# ── `npm run test:e2e` (the default) does NOT need this file. ──
# It runs against the local Firebase Emulator Suite with a seeded fake
# account (tests/seed-emulator.mjs) — no real credentials, no production
# writes.
#
# You only need a .env for `npm run test:e2e:prod`, which runs the suite
# against the real Firebase project (crumb-ddeb6) — for the rare case you
# need to check behaviour against real data. That account must be able to
# open "Manage pre-orders" on the first bakery on the Bakeries page: the
# app's ownsBakery() only allows that for a bakery's registered business
# owner or the hardcoded SUPER_ADMIN_UID, so the super-admin account is the
# simplest choice. (These same two vars are the repo secrets used by
# .github/workflows/cleanup-e2e.yml.)
E2E_EMAIL=
E2E_PASSWORD=

# Point the suite at an already-running server instead of the one it starts
# (e.g. a deployed environment). Bypasses the emulator + dev-server webServer.
# E2E_BASE_URL=
